          "topic": "conditional stat and keyword gates",
          "conclusion": "The conditional block_cost_multiplier uses is_item_slot_wielded and the per-tier override replaces the base conditional value 1 with 0.775/0.75/0.725/0.7. The cost reduction applies while the matching weapon slot is wielded and does not require active blocking; after switching away, the held-slot condition prevents this item's multiplier and ranged keyword from contributing at the next buff-stat/keyword update. Separately, the conditional keyword inherits the held-slot predicate; check_active_func controls the buff's active/inactive status, not its stat or keyword calculation. Block.is_blocking itself requires an active block state before it accepts the ranged keyword. The parent config reflects this separation.",
